      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Background Removal -> Neutral Gray Portrait Reference\n\nBiRefNet (core node) + gray composite. Run once per character, reuse the PNG.\n\n## Chain\nLoadImage -> LoadBackgroundRemovalModel (model.safetensors) -> RemoveBackground (mask) -> EmptyImage (gray, 8421504) -> ImageCompositeMasked (destination=gray, source=character, mask=BiRefNet mask) -> SaveImage\n\n## Custom backdrop color (EmptyImage node)\n- The EmptyImage color widget IS the custom color option - click the swatch in the UI to pick any backdrop.\n- Default 8421504 = 0x808080 = mid gray (validated).\n- Other useful values: white = 16777215 (0xFFFFFF), light gray = 15658734 (0xEEEEEE), dark gray = 6579300 (0x646464).\n- Keep width/height matched to your source image size.\n\n## Why GRAY, not transparent\n- Transparent PNGs load as BLACK backgrounds in ComfyUI. A black backdrop reads as a flat studio cue and drags the whole generation down (flat/cartoon-ish output).\n- Gray keeps the cutout's \"no environment to preserve\" benefit with none of the dark cue.\n- 8421504 = 0x808080 = mid gray. Set EmptyImage width/height to match your source image (1024x1024 for standard gens).\n\n## Usage\n- Pick your image in LoadImage (Choose file button), Queue.\n- Save the output into ComfyUI/input/, then select it in the main workflow's LoadImage node with Identity = Qwen.\n- A ready-made example already exists: input/reference_gray.png"
      ]
    }
